<title>UK: Flying Flowers surge on trading statement.</title>
<headline>Flying Flowers surge on trading statement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in horticultural retailer Flying Flowers surged on Tuesday after the company made a positive trading statement, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1347 GMT, the shares had risen 44p to 327-1/2p in volume of 575,000.</p>
<p>The company said that pre-tax profits for the current year would be well in excess of current market forecasts after orders for Gardening Direct, the company's mail order bedding plant business, were substantially ahead of last year.</p>
<p>--Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
</text>
